questions.topicMd:
**Prefix sums.** Let `pre[0] = 0` and `pre[i + 1] = pre[i] + nums[i]`. Then the sum of `nums[l..r]` is `pre[r + 1] − pre[l]`. One O(n) pass, then every range sum is O(1).

Extensions:

- 2-D prefix sums answer rectangle sums in O(1) after O(rows·cols) setup;
- prefix sums plus a hash map count subarrays with a given sum;
- if values change between queries, use a Fenwick tree or segment tree: O(log n) per update and query.

Off-by-one is the classic bug: keep the extra leading 0 so `l = 0` needs no special case.

